  "the_result": "Every one of the eleven lipidoids has EXACTLY ONE constitution consistent with its printed formula. For the three-armed members this is not luck: 113 and 306 are symmetric about their central tertiary nitrogen, so the only way to place three arms on two primary nitrogens is two-plus-one and the two choices are the same molecule; 400 has exactly three N-H slots, so three arms fill all of them. The enumeration proves this rather than assuming it.",
